Before implementing any generic UI component, search the codebase (especially core/widgets/) for existing implementations that satisfy the requirement.

* **Icons & Emojis**: Use sparingly in the UI; avoid overly casual tones. Emojis can be used in notifications but should be relevant (📚, 🧠, ✅). Always use Font Awesome icons for UI elements.

```dart
import 'package:font_awesome_flutter/font_awesome_flutter.dart';

// Example usage:
FaIcon(
  FontAwesomeIcons.bookOpenReader,
  size: 40,
  color: theme.colorScheme.primary.withOpacity(0.7),
)
```

Font Awesome provides 30,000+ icons - search at [fontawesome.com/icons](https://fontawesome.com/icons)

**LEGACY NOTE:** `SvgIcons` class exists for backward compatibility only. Do not use it in new features. Do not refactor existing code that uses it.

